@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Dimensões orientadas do editor — 0.12.2
+
+## Defeito reproduzido
+
+Ao abrir o editor de um retângulo 7 × 2 pela frente norte, o título mostrava `7 × 2`. Trocar a frente para leste atualizava o rascunho e o futuro centro do tecido, mas o título continuava `7 × 2`, pois era construído uma única vez com a orientação inicial. O teste novo falha antes da correção exatamente nessa transição.
+
+A semântica permanece a existente: largura e profundidade são relativas à frente escolhida no rascunho. Norte/sul usam o eixo X como largura; leste/oeste usam Z, como o cálculo de `planFinish`. Não se muda a posição ou o tamanho do altar.
+
+## Correção restrita à apresentação
+
+`menu.ts` usa `ObservableUIRawMessage`, suportado pelos tipos estáveis instalados de `@minecraft/server-ui` 2.1.0. A assinatura de dois argumentos de [CustomForm](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/scriptapi/minecraft/server-ui/customform?view=minecraft-bedrock-stable) aceita essa observável, que oferece [setData](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/scriptapi/minecraft/server-ui/observableuirawmessage?view=minecraft-bedrock-stable). O título mantém sua tradução e só recebe novo valor quando a frente do rascunho muda. A observável não é gravável pelo cliente, não possui assinatura nova e não participa do commit.
+
+Restaurar também restaura o título. Valores inválidos são rejeitados pelo fluxo existente. Se a direção fica temporariamente oculta, por exemplo na Cruzeta sem toalha, o título conserva a orientação do rascunho, assim como o próprio valor guardado para uma toalha direcional futura. A aplicação do modelo simétrico continua normalizando o state para zero; nenhuma regra do codec é alterada.
+
+## Preservação
+
+Esta revisão não muda geometria, UV, textura, blocos, colisões, IDs, estados, sessão, rollback ou aplicação do acabamento. A estrutura permanece [Cruzeta 0.12.1](CROSSBRACE_0.12.1.md). Não se produziu outra mudança ornamental sem evidência de melhoria. Aspergillum permanece 1.2.5 e Estúdio 2.3.0.
+
+A comparação do runtime deve mostrar somente a apresentação do título e sua nova importação estável. Não requer novas permissões, APIs beta ou experimentos.
+
+## Testes reproduzíveis
+
+```
+node --experimental-strip-types --test addons/altare/tests/menu.node.ts
+npm --prefix addons/altare run check
+HOME=/tmp/altare-creator-home MCT_TEST_PINNED_MC_VERSION=1.26.40 node addons/altare/tools/package.mjs
+```
+
+Os testes do adaptador de UI verificam quatro frentes, Aplicar, Restaurar, Cancelar, preservação das entradas do mundo, valor inválido, título traduzido, observável somente do servidor, modelo simétrico e retorno ao tecido direcional. São testes de contrato de apresentação, não execução do cliente Bedrock.
+
+### Resultados desta revisão
+
+- Altare: 113 testes aprovados, incluindo 8 do menu; tipos e validação estrutural aprovados.
+- Aspergillum: 107 testes aprovados. Estúdio: 84 testes aprovados. Tipos, documentação e build da raiz aprovados.
+- Creator Tools oficial: zero erros, 2.084 avisos de complexidade já delimitados pela política existente e zero avisos inesperados. Validação offline com alvo 1.26.40 fixado; as consultas de registry devolveram 502, registradas no log, sem impedir a validação. O [relatório completo](../dist/validation/0.12.2/release-summary.json) preserva esses avisos.
+- Comparação dos arquivos distribuídos 0.12.1/0.12.2: 5.386 entradas idênticas, incluindo todos os 414 blocos, 4.700 arquivos de geometria e 265 arquivos de textura. Nenhum arquivo acrescentado ou removido.
+- As únicas sete entradas diferentes são o script com a correção de título, dois manifests e quatro arquivos de texto com a versão do pacote. O delta do runtime contém somente a nova observável e a atualização do título.
+- O arquivo final possui 5.393 entradas, CRC íntegro e conteúdo idêntico aos packs gerados. SHA-256: `2b7576872c69fa94f72130c3ae260ebdceafc906c2428985219782a6da4940a9`.
+
+As evidências locais ficam em `out/editor-dimensions/`: regressão antes/depois, logs das suítes, comparação de preservação e delta de runtime. Uma revisão independente de código confirmou a semântica e executou os testes direcionados.
+
+## Menor reteste nativo
+
+1. Importar BP/RP **[0,12,2]** em uma cópia do mundo, sem outra revisão Altare concorrente, no Minecraft mínimo 1.26.40 e sem experimentos.
+2. Abrir o acabamento de um altar 7 × 2 pela face norte. Confirmar título `7 × 2`.
+3. Trocar a frente para leste/oeste: título `2 × 7`. Norte/sul: `7 × 2`. Nenhuma alteração física deve acontecer antes de Aplicar.
+4. Clicar Restaurar, testar Cruzeta nua e depois Agnus/Floral; a direção do rascunho deve ser preservada quando ocultada. Cancelar não deve modificar blocos; Aplicar deve orientar o tecido como antes.
+5. Reabrir, salvar/recarregar e verificar Content Log sem novo erro de observável. Registrar o hash do `.mcaddon` testado.
+
+O ambiente de nuvem não possui cliente Bedrock. Não se declara que esse reteste foi executado. Os renders CPU 0.12.1 documentam a geometria preservada, mas não representam teste da UI nem substituem o jogo.
diff --git a/addons/altare/tests/crossbrace.node.ts b/addons/altare/tests/crossbrace.node.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d6e8f65
--- /dev/null
+++ b/addons/altare/tests/crossbrace.node.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+import test from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import {crossbraceArchitecture,crossbraceCollision} from '../assets-src/atelier/crossbrace-model.mjs';
+import {atelierGeometry} from '../assets-src/atelier/geometry.mjs';
+import {DESIGNS,JOINERY_DESIGNS,CATALOG_PERMUTATIONS,sharedDesignFor,SHARED_TEXTILES} from '../src/domain/catalog.ts';
+import {planFinish,type Tile} from '../src/domain/surface.ts';
+import {encodeTile,decodeTile} from '../src/domain/block-codec.ts';
+import {customizationFromFinish,customizationFinish,customizationCapabilities,changeCustomization} from '../src/domain/customization.ts';
+import {collectionMaterials} from '../tools/catalog-pack.mjs';
+import {crossbraceInlay} from '../assets-src/atelier/materials.mjs';
+const grid=(w:number,d:number):Tile[]=>Array.from({length:w*d},(_,i)=>({position:{x:i%w,y:0,z:Math.floor(i/w)},stone:0,cloth:0,frontal:0,facing:0,edges:15}));
+function points(c:any){
+ const p=c.pivot??[0,0,0],r=(c.rotation??[0,0,0]).map((v:number)=>v*Math.PI/180),result:number[][]=[];
+ for(const x of [0,1])for(const y of [0,1])for(const z of [0,1]){
+  let v=c.origin.map((n:number,i:number)=>n+c.size[i]*[x,y,z][i]!-p[i]);
+  for(let axis=0;axis<3;axis++){const j=(axis+1)%3,k=(axis+2)%3,a=v[j],b=v[k];v[j]=a*Math.cos(r[axis])-b*Math.sin(r[axis]);v[k]=a*Math.sin(r[axis])+b*Math.cos(r[axis]);}
+  result.push(v.map((n:number,i:number)=>n+p[i]));
+ }return result;
+}
+test('Cruzeta adds seventeen finishes without relaxing either state ceiling',()=>{
+ assert.equal(DESIGNS.filter(d=>d.structure==='crossbrace').length,17);
+ assert.equal(CATALOG_PERMUTATIONS,80000);assert.ok(CATALOG_PERMUTATIONS+9744<=90000);
+ const bare=JOINERY_DESIGNS.find(d=>d.id==='altare:j_crossbrace_none')!;assert.equal(bare.codec,'symmetric');
+ for(let facing=0;facing<4;facing++)for(const [w,d] of [[1,1],[7,2],[8,2],[16,8]]){
+  for(const t of planFinish(grid(w!,d!),{stone:0,cloth:0,ornamental:false,facing,design:bare.id})){
+   const e=encodeTile(t);assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(e.states),['altare:edges']);assert.equal(t.stone,2);assert.equal(t.facing,0);assert.deepEqual(decodeTile(e.id,t.position,e.states),t);
+  }
+ }
+});
+test('Cruzeta carpentry does not change with textile, dye or front direction',()=>{
+ for(let edges=0;edges<16;edges++){
+  const bare=atelierGeometry('crossbrace','none','none',0,edges).doc['minecraft:geometry'][0];
+  const structure=(g:any)=>g.bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('crossbrace_'));
+  for(let facing=0;facing<4;facing++)for(const textile of SHARED_TEXTILES){
+   const g=atelierGeometry('crossbrace',textile==='floral'?'ruby':textile,'none',facing,edges).doc['minecraft:geometry'][0];
+   assert.deepEqual(structure(g),structure(bare));assert.ok(g.bones.flatMap((b:any)=>b.cubes).length<=50);
+   assert.ok(g.bones.find((b:any)=>b.name==='top').cubes.every((c:any)=>Math.abs(c.origin[1]+c.size[1]-16)<1e-9));
+   if(textile!=='none')for(const b of g.bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('drape_')))assert.ok(b.cubes.slice(0,2).every((c:any)=>c.uv.north&&c.uv.south||c.uv.east&&c.uv.west),'open frame cloth has a visible reverse');
+  }
+ }
+});
+test('Cruzeta compiled contours share corner posts and keep diagonal support inside collision bounds',()=>{
+ for(let edges=0;edges<16;edges++){
+  const bones=crossbraceArchitecture(edges).bones,collision=crossbraceCollision(edges);
+  assert.ok(collision.length<=5);assert.ok(!collision.some((b:any)=>[0,7,0].every((v,i)=>v>b.origin[i]&&v<b.origin[i]+b.size[i])));
+  for(const c of bones.flatMap((b:any)=>b.cubes))for(const p of points(c)){
+   assert.ok(p[0]!>=-8-1e-8&&p[0]!<=8+1e-8&&p[1]!>=0&&p[1]!<=14.2+1e-8&&p[2]!>=-8-1e-8&&p[2]!<=8+1e-8);
+   assert.ok(collision.some((b:any)=>p.every((v,i)=>v>=b.origin[i]-1e-7&&v<=b.origin[i]+b.size[i]+1e-7)),`uncovered wood vertex ${p}`);
+  }
+  assert.equal(bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('crossbrace_bay_')).length,[0,1,2,3].filter(s=>edges&(1<<s)).length);
+ }
+ const isolated=crossbraceArchitecture(15).bones;assert.equal(isolated.filter((b:any)=>b.name.includes('_corner_')).length,4);assert.ok(!isolated.some((b:any)=>b.name.includes('_half_')));
+ const continuous=crossbraceArchitecture(1).bones;assert.equal(continuous.filter((b:any)=>b.name.includes('_half_')).length,2);
+ const laps=isolated.find((b:any)=>b.name==='crossbrace_bay_0')!.cubes.slice(2,4);assert.equal(laps[0]!.origin[2]+laps[0]!.size[2],laps[1]!.origin[2]);
+});
+test('Cruzeta materials preserve wood, receive all shared cloths, and have no metallic body or extra relief',()=>{
+ for(const textile of SHARED_TEXTILES){const d=sharedDesignFor('crossbrace','walnut',textile,'none');const m=collectionMaterials(d);assert.equal(m.stone.texture,'altare_atelier_walnut');assert.equal(m.joinery_inlay.texture,'altare_crossbrace_inlay');}
+ assert.throws(()=>atelierGeometry('crossbrace','none','cross',0,15),/no applied relief/);
+});
+
+test('symmetric Cruzeta hides direction while preserving the draft for a later cloth',()=>{
+ const d=changeCustomization(customizationFromFinish({stone:0,cloth:0,ornamental:false,facing:3}),{model:'crossbrace',textile:'none'});
+ assert.equal(customizationCapabilities(d).directional,false);assert.equal(customizationFinish(d).facing,0);assert.equal(d.facing,3);
+ const clothed=changeCustomization(d,{textile:'agnus'});assert.equal(customizationCapabilities(clothed).directional,true);assert.equal(customizationFinish(clothed).facing,3);
+});
+
+test('Cruzeta inlay retains physical scale and shared posts reconstruct a complete motif',()=>{
+ const epsilon=1e-7;
+ for(let edges=1;edges<16;edges++){
+  const bones=crossbraceArchitecture(edges).bones;
+  for(const b of bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('crossbrace_bay_'))){
+   const c=b.cubes[0],uv=Object.values(c.uv).find((f:any)=>f.material_instance==='joinery_inlay') as any;
+   assert.ok(Math.abs(uv.uv_size[0]/Math.max(c.size[0],c.size[2])-8.75)<.4);
+   assert.ok(uv.uv[0]>=0&&uv.uv[0]+uv.uv_size[0]<=128+epsilon);
+   assert.equal(uv.uv[0]%16,0);assert.equal(uv.uv_size[0]%16,0);
+  }
+ }
+ const full=crossbraceArchitecture(15).bones.find((b:any)=>b.name==='crossbrace_corner_0')!.cubes;
+ const halves=crossbraceArchitecture(1).bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('crossbrace_half_0'));
+ const [left,right]=halves.map((b:any)=>b.cubes[2].uv.north);
+ assert.ok(Math.abs(left.uv[0]+left.uv_size[0]-right.uv[0])<epsilon);
+ assert.ok(Math.abs(left.uv[0]-full[2].uv.north.uv[0])<epsilon);
+ assert.ok(Math.abs(left.uv_size[0]+right.uv_size[0]-full[2].uv.north.uv_size[0])<epsilon);
+ assert.equal(halves[0].cubes.every((c:any)=>!c.uv.west),true);
+ assert.equal(halves[1].cubes.every((c:any)=>!c.uv.east),true);
+});
+
+test('Cruzeta square recessed shafts meet lower rails and every X has one contained through-peg',()=>{
+ const bones=crossbraceArchitecture(15).bones,post=bones.find((b:any)=>b.name==='crossbrace_corner_0')!.cubes;
+ assert.ok(Math.abs(post[1].size[0]-1.36)<1e-9);assert.ok(Math.abs(post[1].size[2]-1.36)<1e-9);
+ const low=bones.find((b:any)=>b.name==='crossbrace_bay_0')!.cubes[1];
+ assert.ok(Math.abs(low.origin[0]-(post[1].origin[0]+post[1].size[0]))<1e-9);
+ for(let edges=0;edges<16;edges++)for(const b of crossbraceArchitecture(edges).bones.filter((b:any)=>b.name.startsWith('crossbrace_bay_'))){
+  assert.equal(b.cubes.length,5);
+  const [a,c,pin]=b.cubes.slice(2),center=(box:any)=>box.pivot;
+  assert.ok(Math.abs(Math.hypot(...center(a).map((n:number,i:number)=>n-center(pin)[i]))-.24)<1e-8);
+  assert.ok(Math.abs(Math.hypot(...center(c).map((n:number,i:number)=>n-center(pin)[i]))-.24)<1e-8);
+  assert.equal(Object.values(pin.uv).filter((f:any)=>f.material_instance==='joinery_inlay').length,2);
+ }
+});
+
+
+test('Cruzeta marquetry repeats on whole texture pixels without uneven broken diamonds',()=>{
+ const light=(x:number,y:number)=>crossbraceInlay(2*x+.5,2*y+.5).rgb[0]===181;
+ for(let y=0;y<64;y++)for(let x=0;x<8;x++)for(let period=1;period<8;period++)assert.equal(light(x,y),light(x+period*8,y));
+ for(let y=0;y<64;y++)for(let x=0;x<64;x++){const p=crossbraceInlay(2*x+.5,2*y+.5);assert.equal(p.metal,0);assert.equal(p.alpha??255,255);}
+});
diff --git a/addons/altare/tests/editor-timeout.node.ts b/addons/altare/tests/editor-timeout.node.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..171a507
--- /dev/null
+++ b/addons/altare/tests/editor-timeout.node.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+import test from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import {build} from 'esbuild';
+import {fileURLToPath} from 'node:url';
+
+// New, targeted infrastructure regression. The timer/session/edit path is real;
+// the UI adapter only models its documented close/undefined contract.
+const origin={x:0,y:0,z:0};
+const tile={position:origin,stone:0,cloth:0,frontal:0,facing:0,edges:15};
+let writes=0,nextTimer=1,view:any;
+const messages:string[]=[],timers=new Map<number,{callback:()=>void,delay:number}>();
+const system={currentTick:0,runTimeout(callback:()=>void,delay:number){const id=nextTimer++;timers.set(id,{callback,delay});return id;},clearRun(id:number){timers.delete(id);}};
+class Port {
+ read(p:any){return p.x===0&&p.y===0&&p.z===0?structuredClone(tile):null;}
+ reconcile(){}
+ prepare(){}
+ write(){writes++;}
+}
+async function chooseFinish(_player:any,_tiles:any,_facing:any,isCurrent:()=>boolean,onRelease:(callback:()=>void)=>()=>void){
+ let close!:()=>void;
+ const wait=new Promise<undefined>(resolve=>{close=()=>resolve(undefined);});
+ view={showing:true,isCurrent,close:()=>{view.showing=false;close();}};
+ const unsubscribe=onRelease(view.close);
+ try{return await wait;}finally{unsubscribe();}
+}
+(globalThis as any).__altareExpiryAdapter={system,GameMode:{Creative:'creative',Survival:'survival'},BedrockSurfacePort:Port,TOOL:'altare:finish_tool',chooseFinish,tell:(_player:any,key:string)=>messages.push(key)};
+const bundled=await build({entryPoints:[fileURLToPath(new URL('../src/infrastructure/editor.ts',import.meta.url))],bundle:true,format:'esm',platform:'node',write:false,plugins:[{
+ name:'expiry-adapters',setup(b){
+  b.onResolve({filter:/^@minecraft\/server$|^\.\/surface-port\.ts$|^\.\.\/presentation\/menu\.ts$/},args=>({path:args.path,namespace:'expiry'}));
+  b.onLoad({filter:/.*/,namespace:'expiry'},()=>({contents:'export const {system,GameMode,BedrockSurfacePort,TOOL,chooseFinish,tell}=globalThis.__altareExpiryAdapter;'}));
+ },
+}]});
+const {edit,sessions}=await import('data:text/javascript;base64,'+Buffer.from(bundled.outputFiles[0]!.text).toString('base64'));
+const player={id:'expiry-review',isValid:true,getGameMode:()=> 'creative'},dimension={id:'overworld'};
+function start(){messages.length=0;writes=0;system.currentTick=0;assert.equal(timers.size,0);return edit(player,dimension,origin);}
+
+test('scheduled expiry explains closure once without applying the draft or retaining a lock',async()=>{
+ const pending=start();assert.equal(view.showing,true);assert.deepEqual(messages,[]);
+ const timer=[...timers.values()][0]!;assert.equal(timer.delay,1200);
+ system.currentTick=1200;timer.callback();await pending;
+ assert.equal(view.showing,false);assert.deepEqual(messages,['error.expired']);assert.equal(writes,0);assert.equal(timers.size,0);
+ const replacement=sessions.acquire(player.id,dimension.id,['0,0,0'],1201);assert.ok(replacement);sessions.release(replacement);
+});
+
+test('a lease discovered expired by an interaction gets the same notice before the timer fires',async()=>{
+ const pending=start();system.currentTick=1200;assert.equal(view.isCurrent(),false);await pending;
+ assert.deepEqual(messages,['error.expired']);assert.equal(writes,0);assert.equal(timers.size,0);
+});
+
+test('voluntary cancellation before the deadline does not show an expiry warning',async()=>{
+ const pending=start();system.currentTick=100;view.close();await pending;
+ assert.deepEqual(messages,[]);assert.equal(writes,0);assert.equal(timers.size,0);
+});
+
+test('non-timeout invalidation before the deadline keeps its existing silent dismissal',async()=>{
+ const pending=start();system.currentTick=100;sessions.invalidate(dimension.id,'0,0,0');await pending;
+ assert.equal(view.showing,false);assert.deepEqual(messages,[]);assert.equal(writes,0);assert.equal(timers.size,0);
+});
diff --git a/addons/altare/tools/capture-cpu.mjs b/addons/altare/tools/capture-cpu.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10bf6e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/addons/altare/tools/capture-cpu.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+/** Fallback diagnostic, no browser/WebGL. Uses the project's actual geometry adapter. */
+import fs from 'node:fs';
+import path from 'node:path';
+import crypto from 'node:crypto';
+import {spawnSync} from 'node:child_process';
+import * as THREE from '../../../viewer-3d/node_modules/three/build/three.module.js';
+import {buildBedrockGeometry} from '../../../viewer-3d/src/shared/bedrock-geometry.js';
+import {blockPreviewGeometry} from './block-preview-basis.mjs';
+import {planFinish} from '../src/domain/surface.ts';
+import {encodeTile} from '../src/domain/block-codec.ts';
+import {sharedDesignFor} from '../src/domain/catalog.ts';
+const root=path.resolve(import.meta.dirname,'..'),args=process.argv.slice(2),matrix=args.includes('--matrix');
+const outArg=args.indexOf('--out'),out=outArg<0?path.join(root,matrix?'out/crossbrace-cpu-polish':'out/crossbrace-cpu'):path.resolve(args[outArg+1]);fs.mkdirSync(out,{recursive:true});
+const read=p=>JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root,p),'utf8')),atlas=read('packs/resource/textures/terrain_texture.json').texture_data;
+const version=read('package.json').version;
+if(read('packs/behavior/manifest.json').header.version.join('.')!==version||read('packs/resource/manifest.json').header.version.join('.')!==version||read('out/build-manifest.json').version!==version)throw Error('CPU preview requires a matching complete build.');
+const scenes=[{id:'crossbrace-3x2-bare',w:3,d:2,textile:'none',direction:[-.52,.38,-1]}, {id:'crossbrace-7x2-linen',w:7,d:2,textile:'linen_short',direction:[-.45,.38,-1]}, {id:'crossbrace-8x2-floral',w:8,d:2,textile:'floral',color:'green',direction:[-.45,.38,-1]}, {id:'crossbrace-detail',w:1,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[-.65,.25,-1]}, {id:'crossbrace-7x2-bare',w:7,d:2,textile:'none',direction:[-.45,.38,-1]}, {id:'crossbrace-7x2-lace',w:7,d:2,textile:'lace',direction:[-.45,.38,-1]}];
+if(matrix){
+ for(const textile of ['none','linen_short','linen_long','gold_short','gold_long','lace','agnus','verdant','requiem'])scenes.push({id:`textile-${textile}`,w:3,d:2,textile,direction:[-.45,.22,-1]});
+ for(const color of ['white','red','green','purple','rose','black','gold','silver'])scenes.push({id:`floral-${color}`,w:4,d:2,textile:'floral',color,direction:[-.45,.22,-1]});
+ scenes.push(
+  {id:'join-front',w:2,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[0,.02,-1],center:[.5,.5,-.44],frame:[1.8,1.1]},
+  {id:'join-back',w:2,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[0,.02,1],center:[.5,.5,.44],frame:[1.8,1.1]},
+  {id:'cross-front-grazing',w:1,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[-.85,.08,-.5]},
+  {id:'cross-back-grazing',w:1,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[.85,.08,.5]},
+  {id:'corner-underside',w:1,d:1,textile:'none',direction:[-.65,-.5,-1]},
+  {id:'narrow-1x3',w:1,d:3,textile:'none',direction:[-1,.25,-.35]},
+  {id:'square-2x2',w:2,d:2,textile:'none',direction:[-.65,.4,-1]},
+  {id:'side-linen-long',w:1,d:2,textile:'linen_long',direction:[1,.18,.3]},
+  ...[0,1,2,3].map(facing=>({id:`floral-facing-${facing}`,w:3,d:2,textile:'floral',color:'purple',facing,direction:[-.45,.28,-1]})),
+ );
+}
+const onlyArg=args.indexOf('--only');if(onlyArg>=0){const id=args[onlyArg+1];if(!scenes.some(s=>s.id===id))throw Error(`Unknown CPU scene: ${id}`);scenes.splice(0,scenes.length,...scenes.filter(s=>s.id===id));}
+const hashes={};
+for(const scene of scenes){
+ const design=sharedDesignFor('crossbrace','walnut',scene.textile,'none',scene.color??'red'),meshes=[];
+ const tiles=planFinish(Array.from({length:scene.w*scene.d},(_,i)=>({position:{x:i%scene.w,y:0,z:Math.floor(i/scene.w)},stone:0,cloth:0,frontal:0,facing:0,edges:15})),{stone:0,cloth:0,ornamental:false,facing:scene.facing??0,design:design.id});
+ for(const tile of tiles){
+  const e=encodeTile(tile),block=read(`packs/behavior/blocks/${e.id.split(':')[1]}.block.json`)['minecraft:block'],q={block_state:k=>e.states[k]};
+  const component=Object.assign({},block.components,...block.permutations.filter(p=>Function('q',`return ${p.condition}`)(q)).map(p=>p.components));
+  const geomPath=`packs/resource/models/blocks/${component['minecraft:geometry'].identifier.replace('geometry.altare.','')}.geo.json`,doc=read(geomPath),g=blockPreviewGeometry(doc['minecraft:geometry'][0]);
+  hashes[geomPath]=crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root,geomPath))).digest('hex');
+  const palette={named:{}};
+  for(const [name,m] of Object.entries(component['minecraft:material_instances'])){
+   const file='packs/resource/'+atlas[m.texture].textures[0]+'.png',material=new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial();material.userData.file=path.join(root,file);
+   hashes[file]=crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(material.userData.file)).digest('hex');
+   if(name==='*')palette.default=material;else palette.named[name]=material;
+  }
+  const built=buildBedrockGeometry(g,{identifier:g.description.identifier,textureWidth:128,textureHeight:128,formatVersion:doc.format_version},palette,{includePivots:false,includeLocators:false});
+  for(const [name,group] of built.boneGroups)group.visible=component['minecraft:geometry'].bone_visibility[name]??true;
+  built.root.position.set(tile.position.x,0,tile.position.z);built.root.updateMatrixWorld(true);
+  built.root.traverseVisible(o=>{if(!o.isMesh)return;const p=o.geometry.attributes.position,uv=o.geometry.attributes.uv,idx=o.geometry.index;
+   for(const group of o.geometry.groups){const material=Array.isArray(o.material)?o.material[group.materialIndex]:o.material;
+    if(!material?.userData.file)continue;
+    for(let i=group.start;i<group.start+group.count;i+=3){const points=[],coords=[];
+     for(let j=0;j<3;j++){const k=idx?idx.getX(i+j):i+j,vertex=new THREE.Vector3().fromBufferAttribute(p,k).applyMatrix4(o.matrixWorld);points.push(vertex.toArray());coords.push([uv.getX(k),uv.getY(k)]);}
+     meshes.push({points,uv:coords,texture:material.userData.file});
+    }
+   }
+  });
+ }
+ const file=path.join(out,scene.id+'.scene.json');fs.writeFileSync(file,JSON.stringify({...scene,version,triangles:meshes}));
+ const proc=spawnSync('python',[path.join(import.meta.dirname,'cpu-rasterize.py'),file,path.join(out,scene.id+'.png')],{stdio:'inherit'});if(proc.status!==0)throw Error('CPU rasterizer failed');
+}
+fs.writeFileSync(path.join(out,'manifest.json'),JSON.stringify({version,renderer:'CPU barycentric rasterization of shared buildBedrockGeometry meshes',limitation:'Alternative technical preview. No WebGL, PBR, game lighting or Minecraft parity. Official Chromium renderer unavailable in this execution environment.',cameraConvention:'right-handed; direction centre to camera; right = worldUp cross direction',rendererSources:Object.fromEntries(['tools/capture-cpu.mjs','tools/cpu-rasterize.py','tools/block-preview-basis.mjs','../../viewer-3d/src/shared/bedrock-geometry.js','../../viewer-3d/src/shared/bedrock-uv.js'].map(p=>[p,crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(root,p))).digest('hex')])),sourceHashes:hashes,scenes:scenes.map(s=>({...s,file:s.id+'.png'}))},null,2)+'\n');
+console.log(out);
diff --git a/addons/altare/tools/cpu-rasterize.py b/addons/altare/tools/cpu-rasterize.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..11348b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/addons/altare/tools/cpu-rasterize.py
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+"""Technical color-only preview; no browser, GPU, network or external process."""
+import json,sys
+from pathlib import Path
+import numpy as np
+from PIL import Image,ImageDraw,ImageFont
+def camera_basis(vector):
+ # direction is centre -> camera. The basis must have determinant +1;
+ # crossing in the opposite order would mirror lettering and every world X.
+ direction=np.array(vector,float);direction/=np.linalg.norm(direction)
+ right=np.cross([0,1,0],direction);right/=np.linalg.norm(right);up=np.cross(direction,right)
+ assert np.linalg.det(np.stack([right,up,direction]))>.999999
+ return right,up,direction
+
+if sys.argv[1:]==['--test-camera']:
+ for vector in [[0,.02,-1],[0,.02,1],[-.45,.28,-1],[1,.18,.3],[-.65,-.5,-1]]:
+  r,u,d=camera_basis(vector)
+  assert abs(r@u)<1e-9 and abs(r@d)<1e-9 and abs(u@d)<1e-9
+  assert u[1]>0 # screen Y uses minus this projection: world +Y is up
+  if vector[0]==0:assert (r[0]<0)==(vector[2]<0)
+ print('CPU camera: 5 right-handed bases; north +X left, south +X right, +Y up.')
+ sys.exit(0)
+
+s=json.loads(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text()); W,H=2000,1100
+image=np.zeros((H,W,3),dtype=np.float64);image[:]=[232,227,215];zbuffer=np.full((H,W),-np.inf)
+right,up,direction=camera_basis(s['direction'])
+center=np.array(s.get('center',[(s['w']-1)/2,.50,(s['d']-1)/2]))
+allpts=np.array([p for t in s['triangles'] for p in t['points']]);proj=np.stack([(allpts-center)@right,(allpts-center)@up],1)
+frame=s.get('frame',[np.ptp(proj[:,0]),np.ptp(proj[:,1])]);scale=min((W-220)/frame[0],(H-270)/frame[1]);offset=np.array([W/2,H/2+55])
+light=np.array([-.4,.85,-.55]);light/=np.linalg.norm(light)
+textures={}
+for t in s['triangles']:
+ p=np.array(t['points']);uv=np.array(t['uv']);pp=p-center
+ screen=np.stack([pp@right,-pp@up],1)*scale+offset;depth=pp@direction
+ a,b,c=screen;den=(b[1]-c[1])*(a[0]-c[0])+(c[0]-b[0])*(a[1]-c[1])
+ if abs(den)<1e-8:continue
+ x0=max(0,int(np.floor(screen[:,0].min())));x1=min(W-1,int(np.ceil(screen[:,0].max())))
+ y0=max(0,int(np.floor(screen[:,1].min())));y1=min(H-1,int(np.ceil(screen[:,1].max())))
+ if x0>x1 or y0>y1:continue
+ xx,yy=np.meshgrid(np.arange(x0,x1+1)+.5,np.arange(y0,y1+1)+.5)
+ w0=((b[1]-c[1])*(xx-c[0])+(c[0]-b[0])*(yy-c[1]))/den
+ w1=((c[1]-a[1])*(xx-c[0])+(a[0]-c[0])*(yy-c[1]))/den;w2=1-w0-w1
+ inside=(w0>=-1e-7)&(w1>=-1e-7)&(w2>=-1e-7)
+ zz=w0*depth[0]+w1*depth[1]+w2*depth[2];zview=zbuffer[y0:y1+1,x0:x1+1];mask=inside&(zz>zview+1e-9)
+ if not np.any(mask):continue
+ f=t['texture']
+ if f not in textures:textures[f]=np.array(Image.open(f).convert('RGBA'))
+ tex=textures[f];th,tw=tex.shape[:2]
+ u=w0*uv[0,0]+w1*uv[1,0]+w2*uv[2,0];v=w0*uv[0,1]+w1*uv[1,1]+w2*uv[2,1]
+ tx=np.minimum(tw-1,np.maximum(0,(u*tw).astype(int)));ty=np.minimum(th-1,np.maximum(0,((1-v)*th).astype(int)))
+ samples=tex[ty,tx];mask&=samples[:,:,3]>=128
+ n=np.cross(p[1]-p[0],p[2]-p[0]);n/=np.linalg.norm(n)
+ if n@direction<0:n=-n
+ shade=.65+.45*max(0,float(n@light));rgb=np.minimum(255,samples[:,:,:3]*shade)
+ image[y0:y1+1,x0:x1+1][mask]=rgb[mask];zview[mask]=zz[mask]
+im=Image.fromarray(image.astype('uint8'));draw=ImageDraw.Draw(im)
+try:
+ font=ImageFont.truetype('/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf',32);small=ImageFont.truetype('/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf',19)
+except OSError:font=small=ImageFont.load_default()
+draw.text((64,42),'ALTARE  /  CRUZETA EM NOGUEIRA',fill=(55,44,33),font=font)
+label={'none':'Sem toalha','linen_short':'Linho curto','linen_long':'Linho longo','gold_short':'Linho dourado curto','gold_long':'Linho dourado longo','floral':'Floral IHS','lace':'Renda floral','agnus':'Agnus Dei','verdant':'Verdante','requiem':'Réquiem'}.get(s['textile'],s['textile'])
+if s['textile']=='floral':label+=' '+{'white':'branco','red':'vermelho','green':'verde','purple':'roxo','rose':'rosa','black':'preto','gold':'dourado','silver':'prateado'}.get(s.get('color','red'),s.get('color','red'))
+draw.text((64,90),f"Altare {s.get('version','0.12.0')}  ·  {s['w']} × {s['d']} módulos  ·  {label}  ·  geometria e mapas reais do pacote",fill=(100,88,71),font=small)
+draw.text((64,H-48),'PRÉVIA TÉCNICA CPU · iluminação simplificada · não é captura do Minecraft',fill=(105,90,73),font=small)
+im.save(sys.argv[2]);print(sys.argv[2])
